/-!
# Integral and rational fundamental classes of an oriented manifold

Let `M` be a Hausdorff space modelled on a real normed space `E` of finite dimension `n`, that is,
a topological `n`-manifold without boundary, and let `o` be an orientation of `M`
(`TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation M E n`).

For a compact subset `A ⊆ M`, the local orientations of `o` glue to a unique class
`o.fundamentalClassOn hn hA` of `Hₙ(M, M ∖ A; ℤ)` restricting to the local orientation `o x` at
each point `x ∈ A`. These classes are compatible with restriction to smaller compact subsets.
Along a finite set `Z`, the fundamental class is the sum over `z ∈ Z` of the local orientations
`o z`, each read through excision in an open neighbourhood of `z` containing no other point of
`Z` and pushed into `Hₙ(M, M ∖ Z; ℤ)`. An open embedding `j : U → M` carries the fundamental
class along a compact `K ⊆ U` of the pulled-back orientation to the fundamental class along `j(K)`.

For `M` compact, there is a unique class `o.fundamentalClass hn` of `Hₙ(M; ℤ)`, the *fundamental
class* of `M` for the orientation `o`, whose image in `Hₙ(M, M ∖ {x}; ℤ)` is `o x` for every
`x`. Reversing the orientation negates it. Its image under the change of coefficients `ℤ → ℝ` is
the real fundamental class `o.realFundamentalClass hn ∈ Hₙ(M; ℝ)`. If `M` is moreover connected,
the fundamental class generates `Hₙ(M; ℤ)` freely: `c ↦ c • o.fundamentalClass hn` is an
isomorphism from `ℤ`, so every class of `Hₙ(M; ℤ)` is an integer multiple of it.

A continuous map `f : M → X` carries the fundamental class to a class `f_*[M] ∈ Hₙ(X; ℤ)`, which
is functorial in `f` and depends only on the homotopy class of `f`. A homeomorphism `e : N ≃ₜ M`
carries the fundamental class of the pulled-back orientation `o.comap` to that of `o`.

The fundamental class is what cohomology classes are evaluated on, through the Kronecker map
`TopCat.singularKronecker`, and what Poincaré duality caps with.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.fundamentalClassOn`: the fundamental class `μ_A` of `M` along a
  compact subset `A`.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.localOrientationAlong`: the local orientation at `z`, read
  through excision in an open neighbourhood `U` of `z` and pushed into `Hₙ(M, M ∖ Z; ℤ)` for a set
  `Z` meeting `U` at most in `z`.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.fundamentalClass`: the fundamental class of a compact oriented
  manifold.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.realFundamentalClass`: the image of the fundamental class in
  `Hₙ(M; ℝ)`.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.fundamentalClassEquiv`: for a compact connected oriented
  manifold, the isomorphism `ℤ ≃ₗ[ℤ] Hₙ(M; ℤ)` sending `1` to the fundamental class.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.mapFundamentalClass`: the image `f_*[M] ∈ Hₙ(X; ℤ)` of the
  fundamental class under a continuous map `f : M → X`.

For a compact connected oriented manifold, the integral top homology is freely generated by its
fundamental class. Extending scalars along the flat map `ℤ → ℚ` gives the normalized rational
fundamental-class equivalence `HomologicalOrientation.rationalFundamentalClassEquiv`. Its value
at `1` is the rational fundamental class; a rational coefficient `c` maps to `c` times this class.
The coefficient change uses Mathlib's native simplicial-chain comparison and exact-functor
homology isomorphism directly, without requiring Poincaré duality.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.rationalFundamentalClassEquiv`: the normalized equivalence
  `ℚ ≃ₗ[ℚ] Hₙ(M; ℚ)` on a compact connected oriented manifold.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.fundamentalClassOn_eq_sum_localOrientationAlong`: the
  fundamental class along a finite set is the sum of the local orientations at its points.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.eq_localHomologyMap_fundamentalClassOn`: along an open
  embedding `ι : M → X`, a class restricting to the local orientations is the image of the
  fundamental class.

* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.localHomologyMap_fundamentalClassOn_comap`: open embeddings
  carry fundamental classes along compact sets to fundamental classes.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.eq_fundamentalClass`: the fundamental class is the only class
  restricting to the orientation at every point.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.fundamentalClass_neg`: the fundamental class of the reversed
  orientation is the negated fundamental class.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.mapFundamentalClass_eq_of_homotopic`: homotopic maps carry the
  fundamental class to the same class.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.singularHomologyπ_mapFundamentalClass`: the image of `f_*[M]`
  in `Hₙ(X, X ∖ X; ℤ)` is the image of the fundamental class along `M` under the map of pairs `f`.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.mapFundamentalClass_comap`: a homeomorphism carries the
  fundamental class of the pulled-back orientation to the fundamental class.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.mapFundamentalClass_comap_comp`: pushing the fundamental class
  of the pulled-back orientation forward along `f ∘ e` is pushing that of `o` forward along `f`.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.exists_eq_zsmul_fundamentalClass`: on a compact connected
  oriented manifold, every top-dimensional class is a multiple of the fundamental class.

## Implementation notes

The manifold lives in `Type`. The gluing results this file rests on
(`TauCeti.existsUnique_localHomologyRestriction_eq_of_invariant` and the top homology of a compact
manifold) take coefficients in `ModuleCat.{w} Λ` for a ring `Λ : Type w` in the universe of `M`,
as Mathlib's exactness of filtered colimits of modules is stated in that generality; the integral
coefficients `ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift ℤ)` of local orientations meet this condition in `Type`.

## References

* A. Hatcher, [*Algebraic Topology*](https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/AT.pdf),
  Section 3.3, Lemma 3.27 and Theorem 3.26.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Module Set

namespace TauCeti

/-- The coefficient map `ℤ → ℝ`, from the integral coefficients `ULift ℤ` of the fundamental class
to real coefficients, as a morphism of abelian groups. -/
def intToRealCoeff : ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ) ⟶ ModuleCat.of ℤ ℝ :=
  ModuleCat.ofHom ((Int.castAddHom ℝ).toIntLinearMap ∘ₗ ULift.moduleEquiv.toLinearMap)

/-- The coefficient map `ℤ → ℝ` is the cast of integers to reals. -/
@[simp]
theorem intToRealCoeff_apply (m : ULift.{0} ℤ) : intToRealCoeff m = (m.down : ℝ) :=
  (rfl)

namespace HomologicalOrientation

variable {M E : Type} [TopologicalSpace M] [T2Space M]
  [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [ChartedSpace E M]
  {n : ℕ} (o : HomologicalOrientation M E n) (hn : finrank ℝ E = n)

/-- The local orientations of `o`, as a family of local homology classes, are invariant under
transport. -/
private theorem localHomologyTransport_coe_apply {x y : FundamentalGroupoid M} (f : x ⟶ y) :
    localHomologyTransport (A := ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) M E n f
      (o x.as).val = (o y.as).val := by
  rw [← coe_localOrientationTransport, localOrientationTransport_apply]

section Compact

variable {A : Set M} (hA : IsCompact A)

include hn hA in
private theorem existsUnique_fundamentalClassOn :
    ∃! γ : localHomology (A := ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) A n,
      ∀ x (hx : x ∈ A), localHomologyRestriction (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ))
        (singleton_subset_iff.2 hx) n γ = (o x).val :=
  existsUnique_localHomologyRestriction_eq_of_invariant (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) hn hA
    (fun x ↦ (o x).val) o.localHomologyTransport_coe_apply

/-- **The fundamental class of `M` along a compact subset** `A`: the unique class of
`Hₙ(M, M ∖ A; ℤ)` whose restriction to `Hₙ(M, M ∖ {x}; ℤ)` is the local orientation `o x` at
every point `x ∈ A`. -/
def fundamentalClassOn : localHomology (A := ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) A n :=
  (o.existsUnique_fundamentalClassOn hn hA).exists.choose

/-- The fundamental class along `A` restricts to the local orientation at every point of `A`. -/
theorem localHomologyRestriction_fundamentalClassOn {x : M} (hx : x ∈ A) :
    localHomologyRestriction (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) (singleton_subset_iff.2 hx) n
      (o.fundamentalClassOn hn hA) = (o x).val :=
  (o.existsUnique_fundamentalClassOn hn hA).exists.choose_spec x hx

/-- **Uniqueness of the fundamental class along `A`**: a class of `Hₙ(M, M ∖ A; ℤ)` restricting
to the local orientation at every point of `A` is the fundamental class along `A`. -/
theorem eq_fundamentalClassOn
    {γ : localHomology (A := ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) A n}
    (hγ : ∀ x (hx : x ∈ A), localHomologyRestriction (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ))
      (singleton_subset_iff.2 hx) n γ = (o x).val) :
    γ = o.fundamentalClassOn hn hA :=
  (o.existsUnique_fundamentalClassOn hn hA).unique hγ fun _ hx ↦
    o.localHomologyRestriction_fundamentalClassOn hn hA hx

/-- The fundamental classes along compact subsets are compatible with restriction: for compact
`B ⊆ A`, the fundamental class along `A` restricts to the fundamental class along `B`. -/
@[simp]
theorem localHomologyRestriction_fundamentalClassOn_of_subset {B : Set M} (hB : IsCompact B)
    (hBA : B ⊆ A) :
    localHomologyRestriction (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) hBA n (o.fundamentalClassOn hn hA) =
      o.fundamentalClassOn hn hB := by
  refine o.eq_fundamentalClassOn hn hB fun x hx ↦ ?_
  rw [localHomologyRestriction_comp_apply]
  exact o.localHomologyRestriction_fundamentalClassOn hn hA (hBA hx)

/-- The fundamental class along a point is the local orientation there. -/
@[simp]
theorem fundamentalClassOn_singleton (x : M) (hx : IsCompact ({x} : Set M)) :
    o.fundamentalClassOn hn hx = (o x).val := by
  rw [← o.localHomologyRestriction_fundamentalClassOn hn hx (mem_singleton x),
    localHomologyRestriction_refl, ModuleCat.id_apply]

/-- Reversing the orientation negates the fundamental class along `A`. -/
@[simp]
theorem fundamentalClassOn_neg :
    (-o).fundamentalClassOn hn hA = -o.fundamentalClassOn hn hA := by
  refine ((-o).eq_fundamentalClassOn hn hA fun x hx ↦ ?_).symm
  rw [map_neg, o.localHomologyRestriction_fundamentalClassOn hn hA hx, neg_apply,
    LocalOrientation.coe_neg]

end Compact

section OpenEmbedding

variable {X : Type} [TopologicalSpace X] [T1Space X] {ι : M → X} (hι : Topology.IsOpenEmbedding ι)

/-- **Fundamental classes along an open embedding.** Let `ι : M → X` be an open embedding into a
`T₁` space and let `T ⊆ ι(M)` be closed, with compact preimage `S = ι ⁻¹' T`. A class of
`Hₙ(X, X ∖ T; ℤ)` whose restriction to every point `ι x` of `T` is the image of the local
orientation `o x` is the image under `ι` of the fundamental class of `M` along `S`. -/
theorem eq_localHomologyMap_fundamentalClassOn {S : Set M} (hS : IsCompact S) {T : Set X}
    (h : ι ⁻¹' T = S) (hT : IsClosed T) (hTι : T ⊆ range ι)
    {γ : localHomology (A := ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) T n}
    (hγ : ∀ x (hx : ι x ∈ T),
      localHomologyRestriction (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) (singleton_subset_iff.2 hx) n γ =
        (localHomologyIsoOfIsOpenEmbedding (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) hι x n).hom (o x).val) :
    γ = localHomologyMap (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) ⟨ι, hι.continuous⟩ h.subset n
      (o.fundamentalClassOn hn hS) := by
  have := isIso_localHomologyMap (A := ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ))
    ⟨ι, hι.continuous⟩ hι h hT hTι n
  set a := localHomologyMap (A := ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ))
    ⟨ι, hι.continuous⟩ h.subset n
  -- The preimage of `γ` under the excision isomorphism `a` restricts to the local orientation at
  -- every point of `S`.
  suffices hδ : inv a γ = o.fundamentalClassOn hn hS by
    rw [← hδ, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, IsIso.inv_hom_id, ModuleCat.id_apply]
  refine o.eq_fundamentalClassOn hn hS fun x hx ↦
    ConcreteCategory.injective_of_mono_of_preservesPullback
      (localHomologyIsoOfIsOpenEmbedding (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) hι x n).hom ?_
  have hxT : ι x ∈ T := h.symm.subset hx
  rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply,
    ← localHomologyMap_comp_localHomologyRestriction_singleton _ hι h.subset hxT,
    ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply (inv a), IsIso.inv_hom_id,
    ModuleCat.id_apply, hγ x hxT]

open Topology

variable {U : Type} [TopologicalSpace U] [T2Space U] [ChartedSpace E U]

/-- **Open embeddings carry fundamental classes to fundamental classes**: for an open embedding
`j : U → M` and compact `K ⊆ U`, the map `Hₙ(U, U ∖ K; ℤ) ⟶ Hₙ(M, M ∖ j(K); ℤ)` induced by `j`
carries the fundamental class along `K` of the pulled-back orientation `o.comap hj` to the
fundamental class of `o` along `j(K)`. -/
theorem localHomologyMap_fundamentalClassOn_comap {j : C(U, M)} (hj : IsOpenEmbedding j)
    {K : Set U} (hK : IsCompact K) :
    localHomologyMap (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) j (hj.injective.preimage_image K).subset n
        ((o.comap hj).fundamentalClassOn hn hK) =
      o.fundamentalClassOn hn (hK.image j.continuous) := by
  refine o.eq_fundamentalClassOn hn _ ?_
  rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  have hjx : j ⁻¹' {j x} ⊆ {x} := by
    rw [← image_singleton, hj.injective.preimage_image]
  -- The map induced by `j` carries the local orientation of `o.comap hj` at `x` to that of `o`
  -- at `j x`.
  have hox : localHomologyMap (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) j hjx n (o.comap hj x).val =
      (o (j x)).val := by
    rw [← localOrientationEquiv_comap_apply o hj x, IsOpenEmbedding.coe_localOrientationEquiv,
      localHomologyIsoOfIsOpenEmbedding_hom,
      localHomologyMap_congr _ (ContinuousMap.ext fun _ ↦ rfl : ⟨j, hj.continuous⟩ = j)]
  -- Restricting to `j x` after the map induced by `j` is restricting to `x` before it.
  rw [← hox, ← (o.comap hj).localHomologyRestriction_fundamentalClassOn hn hK hx,
    ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply,
    localHomologyMap_comp_localHomologyRestriction, localHomologyRestriction_comp_localHomologyMap]

end OpenEmbedding

section Finite

variable {Z : Set M}

/-- The local orientation `o z ∈ Hₙ(M, M ∖ {z}; ℤ)`, read in `Hₙ(U, U ∖ {z}; ℤ)` through excision
for an open neighbourhood `U` of `z`, and pushed into `Hₙ(M, M ∖ Z; ℤ)` along the inclusion of
`U`, for a set `Z` meeting `U` at most in `z`. -/
def localOrientationAlong {z : M} {U : Set M} (hU : IsOpen U) (hz : z ∈ U)
    (hUZ : ∀ x ∈ U, x ∈ Z → x = z) :
    localHomology (A := ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) Z n :=
  localHomologyMap (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) ⟨Subtype.val, continuous_subtype_val⟩
    (S := {(⟨z, hz⟩ : U)}) (fun x hx ↦ Subtype.ext (hUZ x.1 x.2 hx)) n
    ((localHomologyIsoOfIsOpenEmbedding (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ))
      hU.isOpenEmbedding_subtypeVal ⟨z, hz⟩ n).inv (o z).val)

/-- The class `o.localOrientationAlong` is the image of the local orientation `o z` under the
inverse of the excision isomorphism of `U`, followed by the map induced by the inclusion of `U`. -/
theorem localOrientationAlong_def {z : M} {U : Set M} (hU : IsOpen U) (hz : z ∈ U)
    (hUZ : ∀ x ∈ U, x ∈ Z → x = z) :
    o.localOrientationAlong hU hz hUZ =
      localHomologyMap (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) ⟨Subtype.val, continuous_subtype_val⟩
        (S := {(⟨z, hz⟩ : U)}) (fun x hx ↦ Subtype.ext (hUZ x.1 x.2 hx)) n
        ((localHomologyIsoOfIsOpenEmbedding (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ))
          hU.isOpenEmbedding_subtypeVal ⟨z, hz⟩ n).inv (o z).val) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The class `o.localOrientationAlong` at `z ∈ Z` restricts to the local orientation at `z`. -/
@[simp]
theorem localHomologyRestriction_localOrientationAlong_self {z : M} {U : Set M} (hU : IsOpen U)
    (hz : z ∈ U) (hUZ : ∀ x ∈ U, x ∈ Z → x = z) (hzZ : z ∈ Z) :
    localHomologyRestriction (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) (singleton_subset_iff.2 hzZ) n
      (o.localOrientationAlong hU hz hUZ) = (o z).val := by
  have h := localHomologyMap_comp_localHomologyRestriction (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ))
    ⟨Subtype.val, continuous_subtype_val⟩ (S := {(⟨z, hz⟩ : U)}) (singleton_subset_iff.2 hzZ)
    (fun x hx ↦ Subtype.ext (hUZ x.1 x.2 hx)) n
  rw [localOrientationAlong, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, h]
  exact localHomologyIsoOfIsOpenEmbedding_inv_comp_localHomologyMap_apply
    (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) hU.isOpenEmbedding_subtypeVal ⟨z, hz⟩ _ n (o z).val

/-- The class `o.localOrientationAlong` at `z` restricts to `0` at every point of `Z` other than
`z`. -/
theorem localHomologyRestriction_localOrientationAlong_of_ne {z : M} {U : Set M} (hU : IsOpen U)
    (hz : z ∈ U) (hUZ : ∀ x ∈ U, x ∈ Z → x = z) {x : M} (hx : x ∈ Z) (hxz : x ≠ z) :
    localHomologyRestriction (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) (singleton_subset_iff.2 hx) n
      (o.localOrientationAlong hU hz hUZ) = 0 := by
  let R := ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)
  -- No point of `U` lies over `x ≠ z`, so the map factors through `Hₙ(U, U) = 0`.
  have h : (Subtype.val : U → M) ⁻¹' {x} ⊆ ∅ := fun y (hy : y.1 = x) ↦
    hxz (hy.symm.trans (hUZ y.1 y.2 (hy ▸ hx)))
  have h₁ := localHomologyMap_comp_localHomologyRestriction R ⟨Subtype.val, continuous_subtype_val⟩
    (S := {(⟨z, hz⟩ : U)}) (singleton_subset_iff.2 hx) (fun x hx ↦ Subtype.ext (hUZ x.1 x.2 hx)) n
  have h₂ := localHomologyRestriction_comp_localHomologyMap R ⟨Subtype.val, continuous_subtype_val⟩
    (empty_subset {(⟨z, hz⟩ : U)}) h n
  rw [localOrientationAlong, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, h₁, ← h₂, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply,
    (isZero_localHomology_empty R n).eq_zero_of_tgt (localHomologyRestriction R _ _)]
  simp

/-- **The fundamental class along a finite set is a sum of local orientations.** For a finite set
`Z` and open neighbourhoods `U z ∋ z` with `U z ∩ Z ⊆ {z}`, the fundamental class along `Z` is the
sum over `z ∈ Z` of the local orientations `o z`, read through excision in `U z` and pushed into
`Hₙ(M, M ∖ Z; ℤ)`. -/
theorem fundamentalClassOn_eq_sum_localOrientationAlong (hZ : Z.Finite) {U : M → Set M}
    (hU : ∀ z, IsOpen (U z)) (hzU : ∀ z, z ∈ U z) (hUZ : ∀ z, ∀ x ∈ U z, x ∈ Z → x = z) :
    o.fundamentalClassOn hn hZ.isCompact =
      ∑ z ∈ hZ.toFinset, o.localOrientationAlong (hU z) (hzU z) (hUZ z) := by
  refine (o.eq_fundamentalClassOn hn hZ.isCompact fun x hx ↦ ?_).symm
  rw [map_sum, Finset.sum_eq_single_of_mem x (hZ.mem_toFinset.2 hx)]
  · exact o.localHomologyRestriction_localOrientationAlong_self _ _ _ hx
  · exact fun z _ hzx ↦ o.localHomologyRestriction_localOrientationAlong_of_ne _ _ _ hx hzx.symm

end Finite

section CompactSpace

variable [CompactSpace M]

include hn in
private theorem existsUnique_fundamentalClass :
    ∃! γ : ((TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of M)).homology (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) n :
        ModuleCat.{0} ℤ),
      ∀ x : M, singularHomologyToLocalHomology (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) x n γ = (o x).val :=
  existsUnique_singularHomology_localHomologyRestriction_eq_of_invariant
    (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) hn (fun x ↦ (o x).val) o.localHomologyTransport_coe_apply

/-- **The fundamental class of a compact oriented manifold**: the unique class of `Hₙ(M; ℤ)`
whose image in the local homology `Hₙ(M, M ∖ {x}; ℤ)` is the local orientation `o x` at every
point `x`. The image in local homology is the quotient map to `Hₙ(M, M ∖ M; ℤ)` followed by
restriction. -/
def fundamentalClass :
    ((TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of M)).homology (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) n :
      ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) :=
  (o.existsUnique_fundamentalClass hn).exists.choose

/-- The image of the fundamental class in the local homology at `x` is the local orientation
`o x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem singularHomologyToLocalHomology_fundamentalClass (x : M) :
    singularHomologyToLocalHomology (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) x n (o.fundamentalClass hn) =
      (o x).val :=
  (o.existsUnique_fundamentalClass hn).exists.choose_spec x

/-- **Uniqueness of the fundamental class**: a class of `Hₙ(M; ℤ)` whose image in the local
homology at every point is the local orientation there is the fundamental class. -/
theorem eq_fundamentalClass
    {γ : ((TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of M)).homology (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) n :
      ModuleCat.{0} ℤ)}
    (hγ : ∀ x : M, singularHomologyToLocalHomology (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) x n γ =
      (o x).val) :
    γ = o.fundamentalClass hn :=
  (o.existsUnique_fundamentalClass hn).unique hγ
    (o.singularHomologyToLocalHomology_fundamentalClass hn)

/-- The image of the fundamental class in `Hₙ(M, M ∖ A; ℤ)` is the fundamental class along the
compact set `A`. -/
theorem singularHomologyπ_fundamentalClass {A : Set M} (hA : IsCompact A) :
    ((TopPair.ofSubset (Aᶜ : Set (TopCat.of M))).singularHomologyπ
      (C := ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) n).hom (o.fundamentalClass hn) =
      o.fundamentalClassOn hn hA := by
  refine o.eq_fundamentalClassOn hn hA fun x hx ↦ ?_
  -- `Hₙ(M) ⟶ Hₙ(M, M ∖ A)` is `Hₙ(M) ⟶ Hₙ(M, M ∖ M)` followed by restriction from `M` to `A`.
  have h := TopPair.singularHomologyπ_comp_singularHomologyMap_ofSubsetMap_id_assoc
    (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) (X := TopCat.of M) (S := Aᶜ) (S' := univᶜ)
    (compl_subset_compl.2 (subset_univ A)) n
    (localHomologyRestriction (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) (singleton_subset_iff.2 hx) n)
  rw [← localHomologyRestriction_def _ (subset_univ A), localHomologyRestriction_comp] at h
  exact ((ConcreteCategory.comp_apply _ _ _).symm.trans (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom h.symm _)).trans
    ((ConcreteCategory.comp_apply _ _ _).trans
      ((singularHomologyToLocalHomology_apply _ x _).symm.trans
        (o.singularHomologyToLocalHomology_fundamentalClass hn x)))

/-- Reversing the orientation negates the fundamental class. -/
@[simp]
theorem fundamentalClass_neg : (-o).fundamentalClass hn = -o.fundamentalClass hn := by
  refine ((-o).eq_fundamentalClass hn fun x ↦ ?_).symm
  rw [map_neg, singularHomologyToLocalHomology_fundamentalClass, neg_apply,
    LocalOrientation.coe_neg]

/-- The **real fundamental class** of a compact oriented manifold: the image of the fundamental
class in the real singular homology `Hₙ(M; ℝ)`. -/
def realFundamentalClass :
    ((TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of M)).homology (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℝ) n : ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) :=
  (((AlgebraicTopology.singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) n).map intToRealCoeff).app
    (TopCat.of M)).hom (o.fundamentalClass hn)

/-- The real fundamental class is the image of the fundamental class under the change of
coefficients `ℤ → ℝ`. -/
theorem realFundamentalClass_def :
    o.realFundamentalClass hn =
      (((AlgebraicTopology.singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) n).map intToRealCoeff).app
        (TopCat.of M)).hom (o.fundamentalClass hn) :=
  (rfl)

/-- Reversing the orientation negates the real fundamental class. -/
@[simp]
theorem realFundamentalClass_neg : (-o).realFundamentalClass hn = -o.realFundamentalClass hn := by
  rw [realFundamentalClass, realFundamentalClass, fundamentalClass_neg]
  exact map_neg _ _

section Map

open AlgebraicTopology

variable {X Y : Type} [TopologicalSpace X] [TopologicalSpace Y]

/-- The image `f_*[M] ∈ Hₙ(X; ℤ)` of the fundamental class of a compact oriented manifold `M` under
a continuous map `f : M → X`: the homology class carried by the singular manifold `f`. -/
def mapFundamentalClass (f : C(M, X)) :
    ((singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) n).obj (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ))).obj
      (TopCat.of X) :=
  (((singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) n).obj (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ))).map
    (TopCat.ofHom f)).hom (o.fundamentalClass hn)

theorem mapFundamentalClass_def (f : C(M, X)) :
    o.mapFundamentalClass hn f =
      (((singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) n).obj (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ))).map
        (TopCat.ofHom f)).hom (o.fundamentalClass hn) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The image of the fundamental class under the identity is the fundamental class. -/
@[simp]
theorem mapFundamentalClass_id : o.mapFundamentalClass hn (ContinuousMap.id M) =
    o.fundamentalClass hn := by
  rw [mapFundamentalClass_def, TopCat.ofHom_id, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id]
  -- The identity morphism acts as the identity; its source is read as `SSet.homology`.
  rfl

/-- The image of the fundamental class under a composite `g ∘ f` is the image under `g` of its
image under `f`. -/
theorem mapFundamentalClass_comp (g : C(X, Y)) (f : C(M, X)) :
    o.mapFundamentalClass hn (g.comp f) =
      (((singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) n).obj (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ))).map
        (TopCat.ofHom g)).hom (o.mapFundamentalClass hn f) := by
  rw [mapFundamentalClass_def, mapFundamentalClass_def, TopCat.ofHom_comp,
    CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp]
  -- The fundamental class lives in `SSet.homology`, which `rw` does not see through.
  rfl

/-- **Homotopy invariance**: homotopic maps carry the fundamental class to the same class. -/
theorem mapFundamentalClass_eq_of_homotopic {f g : C(M, X)} (h : f.Homotopic g) :
    o.mapFundamentalClass hn f = o.mapFundamentalClass hn g := by
  rw [mapFundamentalClass_def, mapFundamentalClass_def]
  congr 2
  exact TopCat.Homotopy.congr_homologyMap_singularChainComplexFunctor (C := ModuleCat.{0} ℤ)
    (f := TopCat.ofHom f) (g := TopCat.ofHom g) h.some _ n

/-- Reversing the orientation negates the image of the fundamental class. -/
@[simp]
theorem mapFundamentalClass_neg (f : C(M, X)) :
    (-o).mapFundamentalClass hn f = -o.mapFundamentalClass hn f := by
  rw [mapFundamentalClass_def, mapFundamentalClass_def, fundamentalClass_neg]
  exact map_neg _ _

/-- The image of `f_*[M]` in `Hₙ(X, X ∖ X; ℤ)` is the image of the fundamental class along the
whole of `M` under the map of pairs `f : (M, M ∖ M) → (X, X ∖ X)`. -/
theorem singularHomologyπ_mapFundamentalClass (f : C(M, X)) :
    ((TopPair.ofSubset ((univ : Set (TopCat.of X))ᶜ)).singularHomologyπ
      (C := ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) n).hom (o.mapFundamentalClass hn f) =
      localHomologyMap (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) f (subset_univ _) n
        (o.fundamentalClassOn hn isCompact_univ) := by
  have h := congrArg (fun φ ↦ φ.hom (o.fundamentalClass hn))
    (TopPair.singularHomologyπ_naturality (TopPair.ofSubsetMap (X := TopCat.of M)
      (Y := TopCat.of X) (B := (univ : Set M)ᶜ) (B' := (univ : Set X)ᶜ) (TopCat.ofHom f)
      fun _ hx ↦ (hx (mem_univ _)).elim) (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) n)
  -- The ambient map of `ofSubsetMap` is `f` itself; its source is read as `(ofSubset _).fst`,
  -- which `rw` does not identify with `TopCat.of M`.
  erw [TopPair.ofSubsetMap_fst] at h
  rw [← o.singularHomologyπ_fundamentalClass hn, localHomologyMap_def, mapFundamentalClass_def,
    TauCeti.singularHomologyFunctor_obj_map]
  exact h

/-- **Fundamental classes are natural under homeomorphisms**: a homeomorphism `e : N ≃ₜ M`
carries the fundamental class of the pulled-back orientation `o.comap` of `N` to the fundamental
class of `o`. -/
@[simp]
theorem mapFundamentalClass_comap {N : Type} [TopologicalSpace N] [T2Space N] [ChartedSpace E N]
    [CompactSpace N] (e : N ≃ₜ M) :
    (o.comap e.isOpenEmbedding).mapFundamentalClass hn (e : C(N, M)) = o.fundamentalClass hn := by
  -- `f_*[N]` lies in the singular homology of `TopCat.of M`, read as `SSet.homology` here.
  refine o.eq_fundamentalClass hn
    (γ := (o.comap e.isOpenEmbedding).mapFundamentalClass hn (e : C(N, M))) fun y ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := e.surjective y
  have hx : (e : C(N, M)) ⁻¹' {e x} ⊆ {x} := fun z hz ↦ e.injective hz
  refine (singularHomologyToLocalHomology_apply _ (e x) _).trans ?_
  rw [singularHomologyπ_mapFundamentalClass, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply,
    localHomologyMap_comp_localHomologyRestriction,
    ← localHomologyRestriction_comp_localHomologyMap (hS := singleton_subset_iff.2 (mem_univ x))
      (h := hx),
    ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, localHomologyRestriction_fundamentalClassOn (hx := mem_univ x),
    comap_apply]
  exact e.isOpenEmbedding.localHomologyMap_localOrientationEquiv_symm x (o (e x)) hx

/-- The image of the fundamental class of the pulled-back orientation `o.comap` under a composite
`f ∘ e`, for a homeomorphism `e : N ≃ₜ M`, is the image of the fundamental class of `o` under
`f`. -/
@[simp]
theorem mapFundamentalClass_comap_comp {N : Type} [TopologicalSpace N] [T2Space N]
    [ChartedSpace E N] [CompactSpace N] (e : N ≃ₜ M) (f : C(M, X)) :
    (o.comap e.isOpenEmbedding).mapFundamentalClass hn (f.comp (e : C(N, M))) =
      o.mapFundamentalClass hn f := by
  rw [mapFundamentalClass_comp, mapFundamentalClass_comap, mapFundamentalClass_def]

end Map

/-- Multiples of the fundamental class restrict to the same multiples of the local orientation. -/
private theorem singularHomologyToLocalHomology_comp_toSpanSingleton (x : M) :
    singularHomologyToLocalHomology _ x n ∘ₗ
        LinearMap.toSpanSingleton ℤ _ (o.fundamentalClass hn) =
      LinearMap.toSpanSingleton ℤ _ (o x).val := by
  ext
  rw [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply_one,
    LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply_one, singularHomologyToLocalHomology_fundamentalClass]

variable [ConnectedSpace M]

/-- The map `c ↦ c • o.fundamentalClass hn` is bijective on a compact connected manifold. -/
private theorem bijective_toSpanSingleton_fundamentalClass :
    Function.Bijective (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton ℤ _ (o.fundamentalClass hn)) := by
  obtain ⟨x⟩ := ConnectedSpace.toNonempty (α := M)
  have hx (c : ℤ) : singularHomologyToLocalHomology _ x n
      (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton ℤ _ (o.fundamentalClass hn) c) = c • (o x).val := by
    rw [← LinearMap.comp_apply, o.singularHomologyToLocalHomology_comp_toSpanSingleton hn x,
      LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply]
    exact int_smul_eq_zsmul _ c _
  refine ⟨fun c c' h ↦ ?_, fun γ ↦ ?_⟩
  · -- Compare the images in the local homology at `x`, where `o x` has infinite order.
    have h' : (c - c') • (o x).val = 0 := by
      rw [sub_zsmul, ← hx, ← hx, h]
      simp
    subst hn
    exact sub_eq_zero.1 (((o x).property.zsmul_eq_zero_iff
      (singularHomologyComplSingletonFinrankIso _ (chartAt E x) (mem_chart_source E x))).1 h')
  · -- The image of `γ` at `x` is a multiple of the generator `o x`.
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (isLocalOrientation_iff _ _ _).1 (o x).property
      (singularHomologyToLocalHomology _ x n γ)
    exact ⟨c, singularHomologyToLocalHomology_injective _ hn x ((hx c).trans hc)⟩

/-- **The fundamental class generates the top homology freely.** For a compact connected oriented
manifold, `c ↦ c • o.fundamentalClass hn` is an isomorphism `ℤ ≃ₗ[ℤ] Hₙ(M; ℤ)`. -/
def fundamentalClassEquiv :
    ℤ ≃ₗ[ℤ] ((TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of M)).homology (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) n :
      ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) :=
  LinearEquiv.ofBijective _ (o.bijective_toSpanSingleton_fundamentalClass hn)

@[simp]
theorem fundamentalClassEquiv_apply (c : ℤ) :
    o.fundamentalClassEquiv hn c = c • o.fundamentalClass hn :=
  int_smul_eq_zsmul _ c _

/-- On a compact connected oriented manifold, every class of `Hₙ(M; ℤ)` is an integer multiple of
the fundamental class. -/
theorem exists_eq_zsmul_fundamentalClass
    (γ : ((TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of M)).homology (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) n :
      ModuleCat.{0} ℤ)) :
    ∃ d : ℤ, γ = d • o.fundamentalClass hn := by
  obtain ⟨d, rfl⟩ := (o.fundamentalClassEquiv hn).surjective γ
  exact ⟨d, fundamentalClassEquiv_apply o hn d⟩

/-- **The rational fundamental class generates top homology freely.** For a compact connected
oriented manifold, rational extension of its integral fundamental-class equivalence gives
`ℚ ≃ₗ[ℚ] Hₙ(M; ℚ)`. No finite CW model is required. -/
def rationalFundamentalClassEquiv : ℚ ≃ₗ[ℚ]
    (((AlgebraicTopology.singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℚ) n).obj
      (ModuleCat.of ℚ ℚ)).obj (TopCat.of M)) := by
  let F : ModuleCat.{0} ℤ ⥤ ModuleCat.{0} ℚ := ModuleCat.extendScalars (Int.castRingHom ℚ)
  let eUnit : F.obj (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ) ≅ ModuleCat.of ℚ ℚ :=
    (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.rid ℤ ℚ ℚ).toModuleIso
  let eH := (TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of M)).homologyExtendScalarsIso (Int.castRingHom ℚ) n
  exact (eUnit.symm ≪≫ F.mapIso (o.fundamentalClassEquiv hn).toModuleIso ≪≫ eH).toLinearEquiv

/-- Reversing orientation negates every value of the normalized rational equivalence. -/
theorem rationalFundamentalClassEquiv_neg_apply (c : ℚ) :
    (-o).rationalFundamentalClassEquiv hn c = -o.rationalFundamentalClassEquiv hn c := by
  let F : ModuleCat.{0} ℤ ⥤ ModuleCat.{0} ℚ := ModuleCat.extendScalars (Int.castRingHom ℚ)
  have : F.Additive := Functor.additive_of_preserves_binary_products F
  let eUnit : F.obj (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ) ≅ ModuleCat.of ℚ ℚ :=
    (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.rid ℤ ℚ ℚ).toModuleIso
  let eH := (TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of M)).homologyExtendScalarsIso (Int.castRingHom ℚ) n
  -- Keep the induced integer action visible in these typed comparison maps. The original
  -- composition uses a definitionally equal canonical action in its tensor unit isomorphism.
  change eH.hom ((F.map ((-o).fundamentalClassEquiv hn).toModuleIso.hom)
    (eUnit.symm.hom c)) =
      -eH.hom ((F.map (o.fundamentalClassEquiv hn).toModuleIso.hom)
        (eUnit.symm.hom c))
  have hz : ((-o).fundamentalClassEquiv hn).toModuleIso.hom =
      -(o.fundamentalClassEquiv hn).toModuleIso.hom := by
    apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
    apply LinearMap.ext
    intro z
    simp only [LinearEquiv.toModuleIso_hom, ModuleCat.hom_ofHom, ModuleCat.hom_neg,
      LinearMap.neg_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, fundamentalClassEquiv_apply,
      fundamentalClass_neg]
    exact zsmul_neg (o.fundamentalClass hn) z
  rw [hz, F.map_neg]
  -- Expose evaluation of the negative module morphism as linear-map negation. This avoids
  -- asking elaboration to unfold the coefficient comparison while inferring the argument.
  change eH.hom (-((F.map (o.fundamentalClassEquiv hn).toModuleIso.hom)
    (eUnit.symm.hom c))) = _
  exact eH.hom.hom.map_neg _

/-- The rational fundamental class, normalized by rational extension of the integral fundamental
class. It is the image of `1` under `rationalFundamentalClassEquiv`. -/
def rationalFundamentalClass :
    (((AlgebraicTopology.singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℚ) n).obj
      (ModuleCat.of ℚ ℚ)).obj (TopCat.of M)) :=
  o.rationalFundamentalClassEquiv hn 1

/-- The rational fundamental class is the normalized equivalence evaluated at one. -/
theorem rationalFundamentalClass_def :
    o.rationalFundamentalClass hn = o.rationalFundamentalClassEquiv hn 1 := by
  simp only [rationalFundamentalClass]

/-- Reversing orientation negates the rational fundamental class. -/
@[simp]
theorem rationalFundamentalClass_neg :
    (-o).rationalFundamentalClass hn = -o.rationalFundamentalClass hn := by
  rw [rationalFundamentalClass_def, rationalFundamentalClassEquiv_neg_apply,
    rationalFundamentalClass_def]

/-- The rational fundamental-class equivalence sends `c` to `c` times the rational fundamental
class. -/
@[simp]
theorem rationalFundamentalClassEquiv_apply (c : ℚ) :
    o.rationalFundamentalClassEquiv hn c = c • o.rationalFundamentalClass hn := by
  simpa only [smul_eq_mul, mul_one, rationalFundamentalClass] using
    (o.rationalFundamentalClassEquiv hn).map_smul c (1 : ℚ)

end CompactSpace

end HomologicalOrientation

end TauCeti
